[door opens]

252
00:11:30,907 --> 00:11:31,865
You each are the state's
key witnesses

253
00:11:31,952 --> 00:11:33,301
in a few cases this month.

254
00:11:33,388 --> 00:11:35,042
Agent Lisbon,
you've got Howard and Ang.

255
00:11:35,129 --> 00:11:37,566
Agent Cho, you've got Ringman,
Daily and Freed.

256
00:11:37,653 --> 00:11:39,524
Freed. Freed bit me.

257
00:11:39,611 --> 00:11:41,613
And be sure to mention
that on the stand.

258
00:11:41,701 --> 00:11:43,180
'Teresa, you remember Howard?'

259
00:11:43,267 --> 00:11:45,313
'He and his syndicate
stole $100 million'

260
00:11:45,400 --> 00:11:47,576
from the online accounts
of thousands of people.

261
00:11:47,663 --> 00:11:49,796
And then he stashed the money
and killed his partner?

262
00:11:49,883 --> 00:11:51,406
I remember him.
The guy's creepy.

263
00:11:51,493 --> 00:11:52,494
Guy's going to prison.

264
00:11:52,581 --> 00:11:53,669
Thanks to Agent Lisbon

265
00:11:53,756 --> 00:11:56,063
and her cool, calm expertise.

266
00:11:56,150 --> 00:11:58,326
That's me, cool and calm.

267
00:11:58,413 --> 00:12:00,458
So glad this isn't a Jane case.

268
00:12:00,545 --> 00:12:02,330
You havegotto tell him,
Teresa, that he cannot

269
00:12:02,417 --> 00:12:04,201
threaten people with bombs
to get a confession.

270
00:12:04,288 --> 00:12:05,637
'No rubber masks,
no monster suits--'

271
00:12:05,725 --> 00:12:07,465
Hey, we have a problem.

272
00:12:07,552 --> 00:12:09,380
BFS got a print off the gun
that killed McTeer.

273
00:12:09,467 --> 00:12:12,079
- And that's a problem?
- Yeah.

274
00:12:12,166 --> 00:12:14,255
Boss, the print is yours.

275
00:12:14,342 --> 00:12:16,257
[dramatic music]

276
00:12:27,094 --> 00:12:27,834
[Minelli]
'Your fingerprint
is on the magazine'

277
00:12:27,921 --> 00:12:30,010
of the murder weapon.

278
00:12:30,097 --> 00:12:31,228
Tell me why I shouldn't
be throwing up

279
00:12:31,315 --> 00:12:33,056
in the bathroom right now.

280
00:12:33,143 --> 00:12:35,015
It's a lab error.
It must be.

281
00:12:35,102 --> 00:12:36,756
They're overworked
and underfunded.

282
00:12:36,843 --> 00:12:39,410
This happened last year
with the LAPD.

283
00:12:39,497 --> 00:12:41,238
Just have them retest it.

284
00:12:41,325 --> 00:12:43,937
Come on!
You don't think I did this.

285
00:12:44,024 --> 00:12:48,158
What I think is, I'm up to my
asterisk in political quicksand.

286
00:12:48,245 --> 00:12:50,247
You and your team are off
the McTeer case, obviously.

287
00:12:50,334 --> 00:12:52,641
I understand.
Are we throwing it to the FBI?

288
00:12:52,728 --> 00:12:53,990
[scoffs]
No.

289
00:12:56,514 --> 00:12:57,689
Hey, Lisbon.

290
00:12:57,777 --> 00:13:00,083
- How about this, huh?
- Bosco.

291
00:13:00,170 --> 00:13:01,693
He knows as much about
the McTeer case as you do.

292
00:13:01,781 --> 00:13:03,086
It makes sense.

293
00:13:03,173 --> 00:13:05,959
And, yes,
I had to pull some strings.

294
00:13:06,046 --> 00:13:08,875
Thank you, I guess.

295
00:13:08,962 --> 00:13:11,747
No, no, don't,
don't misunderstand me.

296
00:13:11,834 --> 00:13:14,576
If you're guilty,
I want you nailed.

297
00:13:14,663 --> 00:13:17,405
I just don't want the feebs
strolling around my offices

298
00:13:17,492 --> 00:13:18,710
asking impertinent questions.

299
00:13:18,798 --> 00:13:20,060
Okay.

300
00:13:20,147 --> 00:13:21,409
So you understand,
I have to ask you

301
00:13:21,496 --> 00:13:22,497
some questions now?

302
00:13:22,584 --> 00:13:23,541
'Nothing personal.'

303
00:13:23,628 --> 00:13:25,717
Absolutely. Shoot.

304
00:13:25,805 --> 00:13:27,589
Hey, everybody.

305
00:13:27,676 --> 00:13:31,114
Uh, well, I bet you wish
you wore some gloves, huh?

306
00:13:31,201 --> 00:13:33,682
- So you have some input here?
- No. Just nosy.

307
00:13:33,769 --> 00:13:35,162
It's okay. He can stay
if he wants to.

308
00:13:35,249 --> 00:13:36,163
I'll stay.

309
00:13:38,905 --> 00:13:41,168
Where were you, Tuesday night?

310
00:13:41,255 --> 00:13:44,954
I was at home, watching
television. Nobody saw me.

311
00:13:45,041 --> 00:13:48,305
- What did you watch?
- Some reality show.

312
00:13:48,392 --> 00:13:49,916
Which?

313
00:13:50,003 --> 00:13:51,831
Cooking show, with the man.

314
00:13:54,094 --> 00:13:55,835
- Oh, yeah. That one.
- 'The angry man. Yeah.'

315
00:13:55,922 --> 00:13:57,140
Oh, I know the one.
That's good.

316
00:13:57,227 --> 00:13:58,750
Cooking show. Tuesday nights.

317
00:13:58,838 --> 00:14:00,230
- 'Yeah.'
- Angry man.

318
00:14:02,972 --> 00:14:06,062
So I can, uh, set up a time
for you to take a polygraph.

319
00:14:07,455 --> 00:14:09,631
[dramatic music]

320
00:14:11,198 --> 00:14:12,373
No.

321
00:14:14,592 --> 00:14:15,855
I didn't kill McTeer.

322
00:14:15,942 --> 00:14:17,682
Nobody said you did yet.

323
00:14:17,769 --> 00:14:18,727
Yet?

324
00:14:27,388 --> 00:14:28,389
Good luck with the case.

325
00:14:30,260 --> 00:14:32,480
[music continues]

326
00:14:34,612 --> 00:14:36,005
Having lunch?

327
00:14:36,092 --> 00:14:37,877
A discussion,
about Lisbon's situation.

328
00:14:37,964 --> 00:14:40,140
Okay, Cho, you say
work the McTeer case hard

329
00:14:40,227 --> 00:14:41,750
screw Bosco and Minelli,
you disagree

330
00:14:41,837 --> 00:14:44,709
and you're not so sure.

331
00:14:44,796 --> 00:14:46,668
I'm just saying, maybe
we should let Bosco do his job.

332
00:14:46,755 --> 00:14:48,670
Stay out of his way.
He's a good cop.

333
00:14:48,757 --> 00:14:50,541
Is anybody gonna go as hard
after this case as us?

334
00:14:50,628 --> 00:14:51,934
I don't think so.

335
00:14:52,021 --> 00:14:53,414
Well, you're assuming
Lisbon didn't kill him.

336
00:14:53,501 --> 00:14:55,372
What if she did kill him?
What would you do?

337
00:14:58,288 --> 00:14:59,942
What would youdo?

338
00:15:00,029 --> 00:15:02,423
Me? I'd walk away.
But I ain't the law.

339
00:15:03,641 --> 00:15:05,382
Yes, we walk away.

340
00:15:05,469 --> 00:15:07,210
- Yeah.
- 'I disagree.'

341
00:15:07,297 --> 00:15:08,603
McTeer went after
little children.

342
00:15:08,690 --> 00:15:10,170
Hey, maybe he deserved to die.

343
00:15:10,257 --> 00:15:11,649
If Lisbon has the guts
to kill him

344
00:15:11,736 --> 00:15:12,955
she has the guts
to serve her time for it.

345
00:15:16,219 --> 00:15:17,525
I'm gonna talk
to McTeer's boss.

346
00:15:17,612 --> 00:15:19,831
- I'll come with you.
- Okay, okay.

347
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:22,095
Look, Lisbon didn't do it
anyhow.

348
00:15:22,182 --> 00:15:24,706
I mean, right?
She's not capable of that.

349
00:15:24,793 --> 00:15:25,968
I'm not so sure.

350
00:15:27,491 --> 00:15:29,493
[dramatic music]

351
00:15:41,636 --> 00:15:44,291
What's up that we couldn't
talk inside? I'm busy.

352
00:15:44,378 --> 00:15:46,075
Thought you might wanna be
outside so you could

353
00:15:46,162 --> 00:15:48,251
express your anger
without constraint.

354
00:15:48,338 --> 00:15:49,600
Why?

355
00:15:51,037 --> 00:15:52,952
I know you lied about the alibi.

356
00:15:53,039 --> 00:15:55,432
I didn't lie.

357
00:15:55,519 --> 00:15:57,173
I don't know what
you did on Tuesday night

358
00:15:57,260 --> 00:15:58,958
but you weren't watching TV.

359
00:15:59,045 --> 00:16:01,569
I didn't lie.
He made risotto.

360
00:16:01,656 --> 00:16:03,832
Now this is insulting. You're
gonna continue lying to me?

361
00:16:08,097 --> 00:16:10,708
[dramatic music]

362
00:16:10,795 --> 00:16:12,928
I can't remember.

363
00:16:13,015 --> 00:16:15,409
I can't remember what I did
on Tuesday night. It's weird.

364
00:16:15,496 --> 00:16:17,672
Thank you. And it's okay.
The memory's there.

365
00:16:17,759 --> 00:16:20,153
We can get it back. If
I put you in a light trance--

366
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:22,459
Like that's gonna happen.

367
00:16:22,546 --> 00:16:23,983
Stop trying to hypnotize me.

368
00:16:24,070 --> 00:16:25,375
What if something
traumatic happened

369
00:16:25,462 --> 00:16:27,682
and you're blocking it out?

370
00:16:27,769 --> 00:16:29,379
I didn't kill McTeer.

371
00:16:29,466 --> 00:16:31,729
Well, let me hypnotize you
so we can be sure.

372
00:16:31,816 --> 00:16:33,557
- No.
- Why not?

373
00:16:33,644 --> 00:16:35,168
'Cause I don't want you
inside my head.

374
00:16:43,263 --> 00:16:45,656
So it turns out you're not
quite done with the McTeer case.

375
00:16:45,743 --> 00:16:47,919
- Funny.
- It's not my choice.

376
00:16:48,007 --> 00:16:50,096
- He'll only talk to you.
- 'Who?'

377
00:16:51,923 --> 00:16:54,404
- Agent Lisbon.
- Hello, Dreyer.

378
00:16:54,491 --> 00:16:55,927
[Bosco]
'Thanks for coming in
and helping us out, Mr. Whelan.'

379
00:16:58,321 --> 00:17:02,369
So, you guys are still
working together?

380
00:17:02,456 --> 00:17:04,023
Still a team?

381
00:17:04,110 --> 00:17:05,676
We're both handling
this interview

382
00:17:05,763 --> 00:17:07,678
at your request, Dreyer.

383
00:17:07,765 --> 00:17:09,419
We just have a couple
questions for you.

384
00:17:09,506 --> 00:17:12,292
Just one, in fact.
Did you kill William McTeer?

385
00:17:16,513 --> 00:17:18,472
I didn't.

386
00:17:18,559 --> 00:17:20,909
Glad to hear it.
How's Katie doing?

387
00:17:22,215 --> 00:17:23,129
She's well.

388
00:17:24,434 --> 00:17:25,566
Doing well.

389
00:17:25,653 --> 00:17:26,784
Healing better than I am

390
00:17:26,871 --> 00:17:27,829
according to our therapist.

391
00:17:29,178 --> 00:17:31,441
Where were you, Tuesday night?

392
00:17:31,528 --> 00:17:33,313
At home, alone.

393
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:35,445
Katie spent the night
at a friend's.

394
00:17:35,532 --> 00:17:36,707
And what time--

395
00:17:36,794 --> 00:17:39,275
- You let him hurt her.
- Excuse me?

396
00:17:39,362 --> 00:17:40,885
I recently read
the incident files.

397
00:17:40,972 --> 00:17:42,539
[Bosco]
'The internal SFPD files?'

398
00:17:42,626 --> 00:17:44,063
How did you get hold of those?

399
00:17:44,150 --> 00:17:45,716
You could have taken McTeer
down the Friday before.

400
00:17:45,803 --> 00:17:47,153
A whole week earlier.

401
00:17:47,240 --> 00:17:48,719
That was not the case.
I didn't have it.

402
00:17:48,806 --> 00:17:49,938
I didn't have any--

403
00:17:50,025 --> 00:17:51,548
And in the meantime,
he attacked Katie.

404
00:17:51,635 --> 00:17:53,028
And you could have saved her.

405
00:17:53,115 --> 00:17:55,465
If I'd arrested him
on a hunch

406
00:17:55,552 --> 00:17:56,945
he would have been acquitted.
He would have walked.

407
00:17:57,032 --> 00:17:58,860
But Katie wouldn't
have been raped.

408
00:18:02,168 --> 00:18:04,083
And thatis your fault.

409
00:18:05,040 --> 00:18:06,998
[dramatic music]

410
00:18:08,609 --> 00:18:09,653
[Bosco]
'Mr. Whelan.'

411
00:18:09,740 --> 00:18:11,177
What?

412
00:18:11,264 --> 00:18:12,961
You swore you'd spend
your entire fortune

413
00:18:13,048 --> 00:18:15,006
in the service of killing
William McTeer.

414
00:18:15,094 --> 00:18:17,357
- Why didn't you?
- I couldn't.

415
00:18:19,707 --> 00:18:22,231
What if I'd been caught?

416
00:18:22,318 --> 00:18:24,059
I couldn't leave Katie alone.

417
00:18:24,146 --> 00:18:26,192
My take? Maybe you just
didn't have the guts.

418
00:18:27,976 --> 00:18:30,457
Go to hell, both of you.

419
00:18:35,157 --> 00:18:37,942
[Bosco]
'Don't worry about it.
He's angry.'

420
00:18:38,029 --> 00:18:39,205
Anger turns you.

421
00:18:40,467 --> 00:18:41,598
Yes, it does.

422
00:18:45,428 --> 00:18:46,864
I wanna take the polygraph.

423
00:18:49,215 --> 00:18:51,130
[dramatic music]

424
00:18:53,654 --> 00:18:55,438
[indistinct]

425
00:19:11,933 --> 00:19:13,543
[keys clacking]

426
00:19:24,032 --> 00:19:26,208
How long did McTeer
work for you?

427
00:19:26,295 --> 00:19:28,384
Uh, couple of months.

428
00:19:28,471 --> 00:19:29,864
His record
didn't bother you?

429
00:19:29,951 --> 00:19:31,561
Nah, freaks work harder,
you know?

430
00:19:31,648 --> 00:19:34,869
They're grateful for the gig,
you know?

431
00:19:34,956 --> 00:19:36,218
Not McTeer, though.

432
00:19:36,305 --> 00:19:37,785
Is that why you two
got in a fight?

433
00:19:37,872 --> 00:19:39,395
Me and him?

434
00:19:39,482 --> 00:19:42,050
No, we didn't get in a fight.

435
00:19:42,137 --> 00:19:44,183
He got in a fight with
his jackal buddy, Dog.

436
00:19:44,270 --> 00:19:46,010
They got in a fight right here
in the middle of the place.

437
00:19:46,097 --> 00:19:47,534
Busted it all up.

438
00:19:47,621 --> 00:19:49,492
So I fired his twisted ass.

439
00:19:49,579 --> 00:19:51,929
I mean, that's management 101,
you know, no fist fights.

440
00:19:52,016 --> 00:19:53,192
So I booted him.

441
00:19:53,279 --> 00:19:54,367
He come back at you about that?

442
00:19:54,454 --> 00:19:56,847
No, he knows better than that.

443
00:19:56,934 --> 00:19:58,762
He knows I'm connected.

444
00:19:58,849 --> 00:20:01,374
Connected, really? To whom?

445
00:20:01,461 --> 00:20:03,767
Oh! People?

446
00:20:06,553 --> 00:20:09,164
So what was it about?
McTeer's fight with Dog?

447
00:20:09,251 --> 00:20:10,818
[sighs]
I don't know.

448
00:20:10,905 --> 00:20:12,689
Could have been about
a million things, you know?

449
00:20:12,776 --> 00:20:14,387
Dog was a utility idiot.

450
00:20:14,474 --> 00:20:16,563
'He's dumb
in ten different ways.'

451
00:20:16,650 --> 00:20:18,739
- Dog have a real name?
- 'Everybody does.'

452
00:20:20,697 --> 00:20:22,743
I don't know what his was.

453
00:20:22,830 --> 00:20:25,659
Oh, those are on special.
Buy one, get one free.

454
00:20:26,790 --> 00:20:28,401
No, thanks.

455
00:20:32,056 --> 00:20:33,754
[female #1]
'People vs. Milton R. Howard.'

456
00:20:33,841 --> 00:20:37,845
'Case number 97T03254,
come on down.'

457
00:20:37,932 --> 00:20:39,586
Agent Lisbon,
we have to talk.

458
00:20:39,673 --> 00:20:41,675
How about you give me
a confession, Howard?

459
00:20:41,762 --> 00:20:44,417
Agent, I-I didn't do
these things they said I did.

460
00:20:44,504 --> 00:20:46,114
Okay? Y-you have to hear
my side of it.

461
00:20:46,201 --> 00:20:48,116
I'll see you inside.

462
00:20:48,203 --> 00:20:49,465
Agent Lisbon.

463
00:20:49,552 --> 00:20:51,162
Virgil, talk to her after.
We're up.

464
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:52,903
Agent Lisbon will not
be joining you.

465
00:20:52,990 --> 00:20:54,122
Is my team okay?
Is somebody hurt?

466
00:20:54,209 --> 00:20:57,473
No. You failed the poly,
Agent Lisbon.

467
00:20:57,560 --> 00:21:01,390
"Significant indications
of deception," they say.

468
00:21:01,477 --> 00:21:04,698
You're relieved of duty, agent.
Report to admin for processing.

469
00:21:04,785 --> 00:21:06,743
- Boss.
- Don't.

470
00:21:07,962 --> 00:21:10,225
[dramatic music]

471
00:21:19,147 --> 00:21:21,628
Signature on the bottom.
Gun and badge in the tray.

472
00:21:35,685 --> 00:21:36,599
[gun clicks]

473
00:21:38,775 --> 00:21:40,690
[music continues]

474
00:21:41,735 --> 00:21:42,823
Here's your receipt.

475
00:21:45,173 --> 00:21:46,609
Have a nice day.

476
00:22:03,974 --> 00:22:05,846
[Dr. Carmen]
'Teresa Lisbon in my office,
talking.'

477
00:22:05,933 --> 00:22:07,804
You must be desperate.

478
00:22:07,891 --> 00:22:11,199
I failed the polygraph.
I don't know what I'm gonna do.

479
00:22:11,286 --> 00:22:14,985
Well, reading polys
is more art than a science.

480
00:22:15,072 --> 00:22:17,684
Ask to retake it.
I can teach you how to relax.

481
00:22:20,469 --> 00:22:22,515
[dramatic music]

482
00:22:24,473 --> 00:22:28,129
My father used to have blackouts
when he drank.

483
00:22:28,216 --> 00:22:30,131
One time, he beat my brother
half to death

484
00:22:30,218 --> 00:22:32,438
and he didn't remember a thing.

485
00:22:34,222 --> 00:22:36,050
The whole way to the hospital,
he couldn't believe

486
00:22:36,137 --> 00:22:37,094
it was him who did it.

487
00:22:38,792 --> 00:22:40,141
'Are you drinking?'

488
00:22:40,228 --> 00:22:42,926
Is that why you are talking
of blackouts?

489
00:22:43,013 --> 00:22:45,059
What I need to know is,
is-is it possible

490
00:22:45,146 --> 00:22:46,974
that I killed McTeer
and blotted it out?

491
00:22:47,061 --> 00:22:48,889
You can't remember
the night of the murder?

492
00:22:50,847 --> 00:22:53,459
Well, don't panic.
There could be lots of reasons.

493
00:22:53,546 --> 00:22:54,634
'Stress or--'

494
00:22:54,721 --> 00:22:56,505
Cops can become killers,
doctor.

495
00:22:56,592 --> 00:22:58,072
- It can happen.
- It's ridiculous.

496
00:22:58,159 --> 00:23:01,467
You didn't even know
McTeer was in Sacramento.

497
00:23:01,554 --> 00:23:04,557
His parole officer
called me last month.

498
00:23:04,644 --> 00:23:06,167
Courtesy heads-up.

499
00:23:06,254 --> 00:23:07,211
Well..

500
00:23:09,649 --> 00:23:13,783
Can memory loss be a result
of trauma? Sure.

501
00:23:13,870 --> 00:23:16,917
Your mind shields you
from the awful thing you did

502
00:23:17,004 --> 00:23:18,658
or even what someone else did.

503
00:23:18,745 --> 00:23:21,704
Child molesters
don't get better.

504
00:23:21,791 --> 00:23:25,055
The killer saved a child's life,
whoever it is.

505
00:23:25,142 --> 00:23:27,057
How do I unblock my memory?

506
00:23:27,144 --> 00:23:30,191
Maybe it will come back
on its own. Give it time.

507
00:23:30,278 --> 00:23:32,367
I don't have time.
You-you're useless.

508
00:23:32,454 --> 00:23:34,630
- You and all your talking.
- I'm sorry.

509
00:23:34,717 --> 00:23:37,416
Until you remember,
I don't know how to help you.

510
00:23:39,809 --> 00:23:41,985
[dramatic music]

511
00:23:48,078 --> 00:23:49,428
Jane.

512
00:23:49,515 --> 00:23:50,429
Mmm.

513
00:23:51,995 --> 00:23:54,084
Oh, hey, Lisbon.

514
00:23:54,171 --> 00:23:56,522
I imagine you want me
to hypnotize you now.

515
00:23:58,088 --> 00:23:59,263
- Yeah.
- 'Mm-hmm.'

516
00:24:01,048 --> 00:24:03,746
Nothing in McTeer's parole files
about any Dog.

517
00:24:03,833 --> 00:24:05,139
No known associates, either.

518
00:24:07,533 --> 00:24:10,187
Black widow...dead one.

519
00:24:10,274 --> 00:24:12,668
[Bosco]
'What the hell do you think
you're doing?'

520
00:24:12,755 --> 00:24:14,322
Killing a spider.
What are youdoing?

521
00:24:14,409 --> 00:24:18,326
You're interfering with my case.
You're talking to witnesses.

522
00:24:18,413 --> 00:24:19,936
You're wrong.

523
00:24:20,023 --> 00:24:22,286
- You gonna lie to me now?
- What's the problem?

524
00:24:22,373 --> 00:24:24,811
Drop the McTeer case,
or you'll be on guard duty

525
00:24:24,898 --> 00:24:27,030
at the state capital,
saluting tourists.

526
00:24:31,121 --> 00:24:32,296
Is that right?

527
00:24:34,951 --> 00:24:35,865
Yes, it is.

528
00:24:39,826 --> 00:24:42,045
- Nice comeback.
- 'You told him.'

529
00:24:42,132 --> 00:24:43,046
He knows the score.

530
00:24:45,875 --> 00:24:47,442
May I?

531
00:24:47,529 --> 00:24:51,098
Thanks. My guy at Pelican Bay
came through.

532
00:24:51,185 --> 00:24:55,450
Uh, McTeer had a cellmate
for two years..

533
00:24:55,537 --> 00:24:56,582
'...nicknamed Dog.'

534
00:24:56,669 --> 00:24:59,193
[Van Pelt]
'Hey, we know this guy.'

535
00:24:59,280 --> 00:25:01,543
That's the brother
of McTeer's girlfriend.

536
00:25:01,630 --> 00:25:02,675
David Charles.

537
00:25:02,762 --> 00:25:04,328
[dramatic music]

538
00:25:04,415 --> 00:25:05,504
[door opens]

539
00:25:09,899 --> 00:25:11,510
It's kind of a mess.

540
00:25:11,597 --> 00:25:12,946
Not at all.

541
00:25:13,033 --> 00:25:13,990
It's nice.

542
00:25:15,557 --> 00:25:16,950
I like those pictures.

543
00:25:17,037 --> 00:25:18,734
Those are mostly
from the last tenants.

544
00:25:22,346 --> 00:25:24,566
Uh, where-where
are we gonna do this?

545
00:25:24,653 --> 00:25:27,700
Ah, interesting.

546
00:25:27,787 --> 00:25:29,658
Let's just do it. Let-let's go.

547
00:25:30,833 --> 00:25:32,966
- No.
- No?

548
00:25:33,053 --> 00:25:34,663
No, I'm not gonna
hypnotize you, Lisbon.

549
00:25:34,750 --> 00:25:36,665
- You're, you're too stressed.
- Are you kidding me?

550
00:25:36,752 --> 00:25:38,667
No, it's okay, shh!
It's okay, alright?

551
00:25:38,754 --> 00:25:41,583
I'd have to make all
the stress leave your body.

552
00:25:41,670 --> 00:25:45,239
Maybe have you count down
from 100, 99, 98.

553
00:25:45,326 --> 00:25:47,110
We'd go round and round.

554
00:25:47,197 --> 00:25:50,940
94, 93..
Listen to me, Lisbon.

555
00:25:52,289 --> 00:25:54,814
All the stress
would have to melt away.

556
00:25:54,901 --> 00:25:59,166
You'd have to feel calm
and relaxed and very safe.

557
00:25:59,253 --> 00:26:02,082
It's just about impossible.
I'm not hypnotizing you, Lisbon.

558
00:26:02,169 --> 00:26:04,780
It's not gonna happen,
so you can just relax.

559
00:26:04,867 --> 00:26:09,480
You are not falling into
a deep, relaxing trance state.

560
00:26:10,394 --> 00:26:12,658
[instrumental music]

561
00:26:14,268 --> 00:26:15,791
Sleep.

562
00:26:15,878 --> 00:26:18,881
Okay. Good.

563
00:26:18,968 --> 00:26:19,926
Alright.

564
00:26:24,495 --> 00:26:26,628
'So you're going down
the steps.'

565
00:26:27,847 --> 00:26:29,631
'Relaxing with each step.'

566
00:26:31,502 --> 00:26:33,200
And now you reach the bottom.

567
00:26:35,071 --> 00:26:36,203
The very last step.

568
00:26:37,639 --> 00:26:39,162
The ultimate place of calm.

569
00:26:41,556 --> 00:26:43,166
How are you feeling?

570
00:26:43,253 --> 00:26:44,820
Good.

571
00:26:44,907 --> 00:26:46,735
Good.

572
00:26:46,822 --> 00:26:49,608
You're gonna remain
in this relaxed trance state

573
00:26:49,695 --> 00:26:51,784
'while we think
about Tuesday night.'

574
00:26:51,871 --> 00:26:54,134
But first..

575
00:26:54,221 --> 00:26:56,919
...sometimes you dance to that
Spice Girls CD, don't you?

576
00:26:57,006 --> 00:26:58,051
Yeah.

577
00:27:00,531 --> 00:27:01,489
I thought so.

578
00:27:04,448 --> 00:27:05,449
Now, Tuesday.

579
00:27:08,278 --> 00:27:10,454
You can watch the whole day
like it's a movie.

580
00:27:11,978 --> 00:27:14,458
Every detail is in focus.

581
00:27:14,545 --> 00:27:16,809
You can zoom
into any moment you want.

582
00:27:16,896 --> 00:27:19,420
You can fast-forward, rewind.

583
00:27:19,507 --> 00:27:22,945
Youare in total control, okay?

584
00:27:23,032 --> 00:27:23,990
Okay.

585
00:27:25,078 --> 00:27:25,992
Good.

586
00:27:28,647 --> 00:27:29,822
What do you see?

587
00:27:31,693 --> 00:27:35,305
I'm finishing up the Form 41s
on the Milbank case.

588
00:27:36,785 --> 00:27:38,874
I feel..

589
00:27:38,961 --> 00:27:40,920
...hungry,
'cause I skipped lunch.

590
00:27:43,052 --> 00:27:45,489
The new guy
in the mailroom is hot.

591
00:27:45,576 --> 00:27:46,752
- Is he?
- Yeah.

592
00:27:48,928 --> 00:27:50,146
Let's fast-forward a little.

593
00:27:52,279 --> 00:27:53,410
Later in the day..

594
00:27:55,195 --> 00:27:56,500
...you're about to leave CBI.

595
00:27:58,198 --> 00:28:00,591
Van Pelt's working late.
She's a hard worker.

596
00:28:02,332 --> 00:28:05,422
She might do well if she manages
not to sleep with Rigsby.

597
00:28:06,554 --> 00:28:07,686
Where do you go now?

598
00:28:09,905 --> 00:28:10,950
I..

599
00:28:13,561 --> 00:28:14,649
I..

600
00:28:17,086 --> 00:28:18,131
Home?

601
00:28:20,133 --> 00:28:21,090
Do you?

602
00:28:22,570 --> 00:28:24,267
Where-where-where
do you go, Lisbon?

603
00:28:24,354 --> 00:28:26,530
I'm in my car.

604
00:28:26,617 --> 00:28:27,923
It's low on gas.

605
00:28:29,055 --> 00:28:30,447
[breathing heavily]

606
00:28:30,534 --> 00:28:33,320
It's okay.
You're in a trance state.

607
00:28:33,407 --> 00:28:35,670
Everything is okay.

608
00:28:35,757 --> 00:28:37,280
- I can't--
- What do you see?

609
00:28:38,542 --> 00:28:39,892
Where do you go?

610
00:28:39,979 --> 00:28:41,720
I...I don't..

611
00:28:42,938 --> 00:28:44,723
It's blank.

612
00:28:44,810 --> 00:28:46,725
- I just see a blank screen.
- It's alright.

613
00:28:46,812 --> 00:28:48,117
It's alright.

614
00:28:48,204 --> 00:28:50,424
[breathing heavily]
I don't..

615
00:28:50,511 --> 00:28:53,383
I don't know where I went.
I-I-I can't remember.

616
00:28:53,470 --> 00:28:54,776
I don't know where I went.

617
00:28:54,863 --> 00:28:56,343
It's okay.
It's okay, it's okay.

618
00:28:58,388 --> 00:29:00,303
I can't remember.

619
00:29:00,390 --> 00:29:01,783
That's a little weird.

620
00:29:03,350 --> 00:29:05,526
[sighs]

621
00:29:05,613 --> 00:29:07,267
I thought you were the best.

622
00:29:07,354 --> 00:29:08,442
'I want my money back.'

623
00:29:09,182 --> 00:29:10,531
Hmm. Yeah.

624
00:29:14,100 --> 00:29:15,971
Why can't I remember?

625
00:29:16,058 --> 00:29:17,756
It's interesting, isn't it?

626
00:29:17,843 --> 00:29:19,322
Yeah.

627
00:29:19,409 --> 00:29:20,454
Yeah, it's interesting.

628
00:29:20,541 --> 00:29:22,151
Hmm.

629
00:29:22,238 --> 00:29:25,067
Well, you know,
th-thanks for trying.

630
00:29:25,154 --> 00:29:26,939
You probably have, uh,
somewhere you need to go, right?

631
00:29:27,026 --> 00:29:28,854
Well, I'm not gonna
give up that easily.

632
00:29:28,941 --> 00:29:30,812
[dramatic music]

633
00:29:33,554 --> 00:29:36,818
I can count on you not to tell
anybody about this, right?

634
00:29:36,905 --> 00:29:38,080
On the team?

635
00:29:38,167 --> 00:29:39,212
Oh, Lisbon.

636
00:29:40,430 --> 00:29:42,084
- Hey.
- Jane.

637
00:29:42,171 --> 00:29:43,346
I just need you to leave, okay?

638
00:29:43,433 --> 00:29:44,565
- Alright.
- Could you please go?

639
00:29:44,652 --> 00:29:45,784
It's-it's gonna be okay.

640
00:29:45,871 --> 00:29:47,002
It's gonna be fine, alright?

641
00:29:48,438 --> 00:29:49,483
I promise.

642
00:29:52,225 --> 00:29:53,792
- Okay?
- Mm-hmm.

643
00:30:04,324 --> 00:30:06,630
Tanya? I got your text.

644
00:30:06,717 --> 00:30:08,545
It said 911.
What's going on?

645
00:30:08,632 --> 00:30:11,635
[grunts]
Oh! hey, help, police!

646
00:30:11,722 --> 00:30:12,811
Relax, buddy.

647
00:30:14,421 --> 00:30:16,162
Yeah, we're clear. You good?

648
00:30:16,249 --> 00:30:17,163
[Cho]
'Yeah.'

649
00:30:19,121 --> 00:30:20,035
You fought with McTeer
in the parking lot.

650
00:30:20,122 --> 00:30:21,471
He beat the snot out of you.

651
00:30:21,558 --> 00:30:23,169
That must have been
pretty humiliating.

652
00:30:23,256 --> 00:30:24,605
So you lured him into the alley
and you killed him.

653
00:30:24,692 --> 00:30:26,259
No, I didn't kill him.
I didn't!

654
00:30:26,346 --> 00:30:28,130
You didkill him, David.
You killed him.

655
00:30:28,217 --> 00:30:30,002
But it's our friend
on the hook for it.

656
00:30:30,089 --> 00:30:32,308
Look, Dog, jail is gonna
be so much better

657
00:30:32,395 --> 00:30:34,093
than what you get
if you keep lying to us.

658
00:30:34,180 --> 00:30:36,356
Look, your friend, the cop..

659
00:30:36,443 --> 00:30:38,880
She's the one who paid me
to bring McTeer to the alley.

660
00:30:38,967 --> 00:30:41,840
Look, I had no idea she was
gonna shoot him, I swear to you.

661
00:30:41,927 --> 00:30:43,406
I never would have taken
the money if I knew it.

662
00:30:43,493 --> 00:30:45,756
Agent Lisbon,
she's the one who paid you?

663
00:30:45,844 --> 00:30:47,410
Yeah, I mean,
it had to be her, didn't it?

664
00:30:47,497 --> 00:30:49,412
I heard you guys already
arrested her for it.

665
00:30:49,499 --> 00:30:51,937
But you're guessing, right?
You never actually saw her.

666
00:30:52,024 --> 00:30:55,157
Well, I didn't see anybody.

667
00:30:55,244 --> 00:30:56,680
It was all text.

668
00:30:56,767 --> 00:30:58,552
The deal was I got Bill drunk.

669
00:30:58,639 --> 00:31:01,642
We went out in the alley to go
take a pee, and then I split.

670
00:31:01,729 --> 00:31:04,558
I heard those shots. I just
started running like hell, man.

671
00:31:04,645 --> 00:31:05,864
'And the next day,
there's ten grand'

672
00:31:05,951 --> 00:31:06,995
in my checking account.

673
00:31:07,082 --> 00:31:08,431
Ten grand?

674
00:31:08,518 --> 00:31:10,172
- 'Ten grand, Sam.'
- I heard.

675
00:31:10,259 --> 00:31:12,479
Ten grand just to lure
the vic in, not even kill him.

676
00:31:12,566 --> 00:31:14,002
This is somebody
with resources, connections.

677
00:31:14,089 --> 00:31:15,438
[Cho]
Someone who's not Lisbon.

678
00:31:15,525 --> 00:31:16,744
Seriously, where's she gonna
get ten grand from?

679
00:31:16,831 --> 00:31:17,919
No offense, boss.

680
00:31:18,006 --> 00:31:19,660
I will have Van Pelt
track the text.

681
00:31:19,747 --> 00:31:21,357
Cho and I will talk
to the guy's bank.

682
00:31:21,444 --> 00:31:23,707
Lisbon, get this
through your head.

683
00:31:23,794 --> 00:31:25,622
You're relieved of duty.

684
00:31:25,709 --> 00:31:26,928
You're not even supposed
to be in the building

685
00:31:27,015 --> 00:31:29,496
and you two clowns
are wayout of hand.

686
00:31:29,583 --> 00:31:31,628
Let me deal with this.
Come here.

687
00:31:37,373 --> 00:31:40,550
Lisbon, look at me. Look at me.

688
00:31:40,637 --> 00:31:43,902
I'll handle it.
Will you please trust me?

689
00:31:43,989 --> 00:31:46,861
I'm sorry.
You don't understand.

690
00:31:46,948 --> 00:31:48,384
Later, you will.

691
00:31:48,471 --> 00:31:51,083
What are-are-are you
medicated or something?

692
00:31:51,170 --> 00:31:53,737
Okay, I'm alright.
I'm fine.

693
00:31:53,824 --> 00:31:57,393
What the hell is everybody
looking at? I'm fine!

694
00:31:57,480 --> 00:32:00,048
Just stay the hell away from me.
I'm done with this crap.

695
00:32:00,135 --> 00:32:01,484
I am done.

696
00:32:01,571 --> 00:32:03,660
Get out of my way.
I'm sick of everybody.

697
00:32:04,661 --> 00:32:06,925
[dramatic music]

698
00:32:16,760 --> 00:32:18,197
What was that, Lisbon?

699
00:32:18,284 --> 00:32:19,546
[Rigsby]
'She's freaking out.'

700
00:32:19,633 --> 00:32:21,287
Oh, come on.
It's just Lisbon.

701
00:32:21,374 --> 00:32:23,811
- She's a little stressed.
- What is going on?

702
00:32:34,822 --> 00:32:35,954
Sorry.

703
00:32:37,607 --> 00:32:40,393
- Why is this happening to me?
- It's alright.

704
00:32:40,480 --> 00:32:43,135
- Let's-let's go home.
- I'll take her.

705
00:32:43,222 --> 00:32:44,571
No. Leave me alone.

706
00:32:57,888 --> 00:33:00,152
[music on earphones]

707
00:33:06,810 --> 00:33:09,161
[dramatic music]

708
00:33:28,615 --> 00:33:30,443
The ten grand paid
to David Charles

709
00:33:30,530 --> 00:33:32,967
came from an account owned by
a shell company in the Caymans.

710
00:33:33,054 --> 00:33:34,186
Well, that's good.

711
00:33:34,273 --> 00:33:35,970
The day after it paid David

712
00:33:36,057 --> 00:33:38,146
the account paid out a million
dollars to someone else.

713
00:33:38,233 --> 00:33:39,887
I bet that's for the shooter.
Can we trace the payment?

714
00:33:39,974 --> 00:33:41,193
Uh, I'm trying, but--

715
00:33:41,280 --> 00:33:42,977
You'll find it dead-ends
in a blind account

716
00:33:43,064 --> 00:33:44,761
that was closed yesterday.

717
00:33:44,848 --> 00:33:47,373
Okay. We are working
the case. We just want to--

718
00:33:47,460 --> 00:33:49,592
Forget about it. How's Lisbon?

719
00:33:49,679 --> 00:33:50,811
She's fine.

720
00:33:52,682 --> 00:33:54,032
She's fine.

721
00:33:54,119 --> 00:33:56,338
Well, what did she say,
exactly?

722
00:33:56,425 --> 00:33:57,905
Well, I didn't actually
talkto her.

723
00:33:57,992 --> 00:33:59,211
She-she wouldn't let me in.

724
00:34:02,518 --> 00:34:03,563
'You're worried about her.'

725
00:34:07,871 --> 00:34:09,221
You think she might do
something stupid?

726
00:34:09,308 --> 00:34:11,049
Suicide? No.

727
00:34:13,529 --> 00:34:15,140
If she did,
she wouldn't blame the bureau.

728
00:34:15,227 --> 00:34:16,750
That's not my concern at all.

729
00:34:18,143 --> 00:34:20,623
I should've taken her
off-duty weapon.

730
00:34:20,710 --> 00:34:21,929
Oh, I'm sure she'll be alright.

731
00:34:28,805 --> 00:34:29,937
[knock on door]

732
00:34:32,374 --> 00:34:34,681
Minelli asked me to drop by.

733
00:34:34,768 --> 00:34:38,250
Well, ordered me
to drop by, actually.

734
00:34:38,337 --> 00:34:40,643
- Can we talk?
- Minelli?

735
00:34:40,730 --> 00:34:41,731
He's worried about you.

736
00:34:43,211 --> 00:34:44,691
We all are.

737
00:34:44,778 --> 00:34:46,736
'Cause I had a meltdown?

738
00:34:46,823 --> 00:34:48,738
Got perp-walked out of the CBI?

739
00:34:48,825 --> 00:34:50,349
'Or because I killed a guy?'

740
00:34:50,436 --> 00:34:51,393
[dramatic music]

741
00:34:51,480 --> 00:34:55,267
Wh...youkilled McTeer?

742
00:34:55,354 --> 00:34:57,878
How the hell would I know?
Maybe?

743
00:35:00,228 --> 00:35:04,276
Uh, Teresa, you-you wanna
put away your Glock there?

744
00:35:04,363 --> 00:35:07,279
Very good eye, doctor.

745
00:35:07,366 --> 00:35:10,238
The Glock, 9 millimeter.

746
00:35:10,325 --> 00:35:13,459
The safety's in the trigger.
How stupid is that?

747
00:35:13,546 --> 00:35:17,376
I mean, it's kind of like
not having a safety at all.

748
00:35:17,463 --> 00:35:18,681
How about you give it to me?

749
00:35:21,293 --> 00:35:23,860
Don't look at me like that.

750
00:35:23,947 --> 00:35:26,472
Don't look at me like that.
This is your fault.

751
00:35:26,559 --> 00:35:28,735
Well, Teresa..

752
00:35:28,822 --> 00:35:31,433
You unlocked too many things
in my head

753
00:35:31,520 --> 00:35:33,479
and now I can't remember.

754
00:35:33,566 --> 00:35:36,917
My head is messed up,
and it's your fault.

755
00:35:37,004 --> 00:35:38,136
Teresa..

756
00:35:39,615 --> 00:35:40,834
...put it down.

757
00:35:40,921 --> 00:35:42,575
'You need to be calm..'

758
00:35:43,880 --> 00:35:45,752
...and put down the gun.

759
00:35:45,839 --> 00:35:47,014
Calm?

760
00:35:49,147 --> 00:35:50,931
You were right, doctor.

761
00:35:51,018 --> 00:35:52,802
There was something
I wanted to tell you.

762
00:35:54,804 --> 00:35:57,851
I act calm on the outside,
but on the inside

763
00:35:57,938 --> 00:36:00,723
I'm so angry, sometimes
I think I'm gonna explode.

764
00:36:02,464 --> 00:36:05,032
All the misery and the pain
that I see every day

765
00:36:05,119 --> 00:36:08,905
makes me wanna scream,
but I lock it down.

766
00:36:08,992 --> 00:36:12,474
I lock it down because
I have to be calm and rational

767
00:36:12,561 --> 00:36:16,174
because that's my job,
but I wanna pull this trigger.

768
00:36:16,261 --> 00:36:17,479
I wanna kill.

769
00:36:17,566 --> 00:36:19,481
You're angry. I hear that.

770
00:36:20,308 --> 00:36:22,354
[dramatic music]

771
00:36:23,790 --> 00:36:24,921
I think I did it.

772
00:36:26,967 --> 00:36:28,838
I think I killed McTeer.

773
00:36:28,925 --> 00:36:32,233
Shh, Teresa.

774
00:36:34,888 --> 00:36:37,151
'If you did it..'

775
00:36:37,238 --> 00:36:38,935
'...that's okay.'

776
00:36:39,022 --> 00:36:41,242
He was a bad man.

777
00:36:41,329 --> 00:36:43,636
No reason for you
to hurt anyone else..

778
00:36:44,941 --> 00:36:47,205
...or yourself.

779
00:36:47,292 --> 00:36:49,816
- I still can't remember.
- You can and you will.

780
00:36:49,903 --> 00:36:53,211
And when you do, Teresa, when
you push through to the truth

781
00:36:53,298 --> 00:36:56,779
all this weight and worry
will come off your shoulders.

782
00:36:58,520 --> 00:37:00,609
Okay.

783
00:37:00,696 --> 00:37:02,742
'I want you..'

784
00:37:02,829 --> 00:37:06,267
...to visualize
that scene for me.

785
00:37:08,138 --> 00:37:10,489
Relive that moment.

786
00:37:10,576 --> 00:37:12,578
You went into the alley..

787
00:37:12,665 --> 00:37:15,102
...after this terrible man.

788
00:37:16,625 --> 00:37:18,279
Can you see him?

789
00:37:18,366 --> 00:37:19,280
No.

790
00:37:21,021 --> 00:37:23,502
Well, yes. Yeah, m-maybe.

791
00:37:23,589 --> 00:37:26,548
Yes. You see him.

792
00:37:26,635 --> 00:37:28,898
You see the dumpsters
and the trash

793
00:37:28,985 --> 00:37:31,901
and the crumbly, old brick,
and you see McTeer.

794
00:37:33,686 --> 00:37:36,210
You see him there,
this-this monster

795
00:37:36,297 --> 00:37:38,604
who destroyed so many lives.

796
00:37:38,691 --> 00:37:40,345
It's too much.

797
00:37:40,432 --> 00:37:41,563
'See it, Teresa.'

798
00:37:44,523 --> 00:37:46,655
[gunshots]

799
00:37:46,742 --> 00:37:48,570
Live it..

800
00:37:48,657 --> 00:37:50,442
...the reek, the garbage.

801
00:37:50,529 --> 00:37:52,705
The filthy alley walls.

802
00:37:52,792 --> 00:37:54,881
The faded cross there.

803
00:37:59,320 --> 00:38:01,801
God might have mercy
on William McTeer

804
00:38:01,888 --> 00:38:04,151
but you sure as hell wouldn't.

805
00:38:04,238 --> 00:38:06,240
He deserved to die.

806
00:38:06,327 --> 00:38:09,852
'But you're still
a good person, Teresa.'

807
00:38:09,939 --> 00:38:11,419
'You can get through this.'

808
00:38:12,899 --> 00:38:14,379
The cross?

809
00:38:14,466 --> 00:38:16,468
Uh, what?

810
00:38:16,555 --> 00:38:19,427
The cross, Roy.

811
00:38:19,514 --> 00:38:21,516
'How did you know
about the cross?'

812
00:38:21,603 --> 00:38:25,041
It was inside the door.
Only the killer saw it.

813
00:38:25,128 --> 00:38:28,784
Well, Teresa, you told me
about the crime scene.

814
00:38:28,871 --> 00:38:29,785
No, I didn't.

815
00:38:31,526 --> 00:38:33,311
[gunshots]

816
00:38:38,011 --> 00:38:41,275
[Jane]
'Oh, beautifully done.'

817
00:38:41,362 --> 00:38:42,711
'Lovely work, Lisbon.'

818
00:38:42,798 --> 00:38:44,060
What are you..

819
00:38:44,147 --> 00:38:46,541
Of course, the cross.

820
00:38:46,628 --> 00:38:49,109
You couldn't resist
the imagery, could you, doc?

821
00:38:49,196 --> 00:38:51,851
- Lapsed Catholic, perhaps?
- What's going on?

822
00:38:51,938 --> 00:38:55,028
Surrender, Dorothy.
We got you. Brilliant, though.

823
00:38:55,115 --> 00:38:57,552
Made Lisbon come back
week after week

824
00:38:57,639 --> 00:38:59,902
so you get her fingerprints
off your coffee mug

825
00:38:59,989 --> 00:39:03,689
and dose her up
with, uh, Lorazepam?

826
00:39:03,776 --> 00:39:06,169
Double dose for Tuesday
to cause the memory loss.

827
00:39:06,256 --> 00:39:09,129
Memory loss you knew
Lisbon would conceal

828
00:39:09,216 --> 00:39:11,958
which made her fail
the polygraph.

829
00:39:12,045 --> 00:39:15,570
Quite the, uh, student
of human nature, huh, doctor?

830
00:39:15,657 --> 00:39:17,485
Well done, really.

831
00:39:17,572 --> 00:39:19,661
Your breakdown in CBI,
that was fake?

832
00:39:19,748 --> 00:39:22,534
[Jane]
'And how good was that, huh?
What about that?'

833
00:39:22,621 --> 00:39:24,710
After that, all I had
to do was get Minelli

834
00:39:24,797 --> 00:39:26,625
to get you to come
around here.

835
00:39:26,712 --> 00:39:28,104
I've been waiting for you
all night.

836
00:39:28,191 --> 00:39:29,454
There was one little thing.

837
00:39:29,541 --> 00:39:32,021
I'm-I'm just,
just one little thing.

838
00:39:32,108 --> 00:39:34,589
The Lorazepam? Maybe
that went a little too far.

839
00:39:34,676 --> 00:39:36,939
When-when Lisbon couldn't
remember the night of the murder

840
00:39:37,026 --> 00:39:40,856
even under hypnosis,
I knew she'd been drugged.

841
00:39:40,943 --> 00:39:43,859
The rest of it? Spot on.

842
00:39:43,946 --> 00:39:45,470
Very, very impressive.

843
00:39:46,906 --> 00:39:49,082
- Thanks.
- Not at all.

844
00:39:49,169 --> 00:39:50,562
[instrumental music]

845
00:39:50,649 --> 00:39:53,129
[grunts]

846
00:39:53,216 --> 00:39:55,958
You're under arrest. You have
the right to remain silent.

847
00:39:56,045 --> 00:39:57,612
Anything you say or do

848
00:39:57,699 --> 00:39:59,353
can and will be used
against you in court.

849
00:39:59,440 --> 00:40:01,529
'You have the right
to an attorney.'

850
00:40:01,616 --> 00:40:03,618
So this guy who gave you
the million bucks.

851
00:40:03,705 --> 00:40:05,011
You ever met him
face-to-face?

852
00:40:05,098 --> 00:40:08,014
You want him?
I want a deal, a good one.

853
00:40:08,101 --> 00:40:09,232
What I got, it's worth it.

854
00:40:09,319 --> 00:40:11,191
Two to five, minimum security.

855
00:40:11,278 --> 00:40:13,454
Oh, there won't be a deal.
We know who he is.

856
00:40:13,541 --> 00:40:14,934
Just curious if youknew.

857
00:40:16,022 --> 00:40:17,893
[instrumental music]

858
00:40:28,687 --> 00:40:30,906
[Van Pelt]
'It took us a while
but we traced the shell company'

859
00:40:30,993 --> 00:40:32,952
'back to you, Howard.'

860
00:40:33,039 --> 00:40:34,867
You paid Dr. Carmen
and David Charles

861
00:40:34,954 --> 00:40:36,869
to frame Lisbon
for McTeer's murder.

862
00:40:36,956 --> 00:40:39,567
These cash transactions
prove it.

863
00:40:39,654 --> 00:40:42,744
Discrediting a cop is so much
smarter than killing her.

864
00:40:42,831 --> 00:40:44,703
'We'd have been all over that.'

865
00:40:44,790 --> 00:40:47,270
But this way, her testimony
dies along with her career.

866
00:40:47,357 --> 00:40:49,055
How about you give us
a statement?

867
00:40:49,142 --> 00:40:50,186
Maybe help yourself?

868
00:40:51,840 --> 00:40:53,407
How about you kiss me?

869
00:40:53,494 --> 00:40:56,236
[dramatic music]

870
00:40:56,323 --> 00:40:58,107
You're pretty.

871
00:40:58,194 --> 00:41:01,676
So are you, compared to
most state prison inmates.

872
00:41:08,335 --> 00:41:10,337
[Bosco]
'I hear Minelli's
billing you for the glass.'

873
00:41:11,556 --> 00:41:12,644
[Lisbon]
'It's only fair.'

874
00:41:15,211 --> 00:41:17,736
You know, for a cop, you made
a very convincing lunatic.

875
00:41:19,694 --> 00:41:21,696
Jane must be proud.

876
00:41:21,783 --> 00:41:23,263
Maybe it's not good police work

877
00:41:23,350 --> 00:41:26,353
but I have to confess,
I enjoyed it.

878
00:41:26,440 --> 00:41:29,008
Letting loose for once?

879
00:41:29,095 --> 00:41:30,313
Look, I'm glad you got cleared.

880
00:41:33,752 --> 00:41:35,797
I'm sorry that we couldn't
let you in on the plan.

881
00:41:35,884 --> 00:41:37,495
You could have, but you didn't.

882
00:41:40,280 --> 00:41:41,411
[sighs]

883
00:41:44,153 --> 00:41:47,287
You should know that
if it turned out to be you..

884
00:41:50,508 --> 00:41:52,205
I know.

885
00:41:52,292 --> 00:41:53,511
Just so you do.

886
00:41:55,425 --> 00:41:56,731
[footsteps approach]
Enough said.

887
00:41:56,818 --> 00:41:58,124
I'm not interrupting
anything, am I?

888
00:41:58,211 --> 00:42:00,082
No. Night, Lisbon.

889
00:42:01,693 --> 00:42:02,737
Night, Sam.

890
00:42:04,217 --> 00:42:05,523
- Donuts from Marie's.
- Oh!

891
00:42:07,176 --> 00:42:09,788
I didn't see it, of course.

892
00:42:09,875 --> 00:42:12,094
What?

893
00:42:12,181 --> 00:42:15,750
- He's in love with you.
- Don't be silly.

894
00:42:15,837 --> 00:42:17,665
I know, hard to fathom,
but, uh..

895
00:42:17,752 --> 00:42:20,102
...there's no accounting
for taste, is there?

896
00:42:20,189 --> 00:42:21,147
Hush!

897
00:42:27,849 --> 00:42:29,895
[instrumental music]

898
00:42:43,125 --> 00:42:45,563
[Jane]
Stay tuned for scenes
from our next episode.

899
00:42:49,218 --> 00:42:50,437
[theme music]

